Zero Trust Network Access (ZTNA)

ZTNA establishes a secure session between an end entity and network, while ensuring granular
control over access to resources and exercising zero trust, regardless of the location of 
either the end entity or the network

- Zero trust: Least privilege access
- Automatic encrypted tunnels:
    - End entity to the ZNTA access proxy
    - Hidden resources
- Components:
    - ZTNA client (can be used with a web browser)
    - ZTNA access proxy
    - Authentication-on-premises directory server or identity-as-a-service (IDaaS)
    - Security-ZTNA policy server and firewall
- Dynamic access control
    - Granular, per-session access : This means that each time the user connects to the network,
      the user is authenticated and a risk assessment is completed on the connecting device
    - Based on:
      - User identity
      - Device identity and risk profile: A device could be a computer or a handheld device
      - Policy: Plocy can define access parameters to resources, based on user role, device type,
        and other factors

Unlike IPsec VPN, but similar to SSL VPN, ZTNA is vendor specific.
This means that each vendor can implement ZTNA in a way that best suits their specific requirements.
